"task_type": "Judgment", "input": "Can ocean big data technology replace humans in conducting marine science research?", "output": "Oceanic big data technology is a technical method to aid oceanographic research. Although it performs outstandingly in certain fields, it still requires human intelligence for analysis and judgement, and therefore, it cannot fully replace human involvement in ocean science research."}\n{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "Elucidate the current status and changes in the marine environment.", "output": "Due to human activities and climate change, the current situation and changes in the marine environment are becoming increasingly severe. This includes seawater pollution, ocean warming and acidification, sea-level rise, and so on. To achieve sustainable development of the oceans, it is necessary to strengthen protection and governance, and enhance environmental adaptability."}\n', 'reference': '1 inch = 25.4 millimeters, you need to convert the diameter of the submarine cable into millimeters by multiplying it by 25.4.'}{'question': 'Into which categories is marine energy divided according to its source?', 'answer': "\n\nMarine energy is divided into the following categories based on its source:  \n1. **Ocean wind energy** (converting kinetic energy from seawater using marine wind turbines).  \n2. **Ocean tidal energy** (utilizing tidal currents caused by the Earth's rotation and tidal changes).  \n3. **Ocean wave energy** (harnessing kinetic energy from surface water waves).  \n4. **Ocean thermal energy** (converting temperature differences in seawater).  \n5. **Ocean biomass energy** (using biomass like seaweed for energy production).  \n\nThis classification is derived from the provided context.", 'contexts': 'ispute not only impacts maritime resources utilization and freedom of navigation, but also affects political and economic matters among the regions."}{"task_type": "Transformation", "input": "How can the application of marine energy technology be divided into different aspects?", "output": "The application of maritime energy technology can be divided into several aspects: ocean wind energy, ocean tidal energy, ocean wave energy, ocean thermal energy, and ocean biomass energy, etc. Among these, ocean wind energy transforms the kinetic energy in seawater into electrical energy through marine wind turbines; Ocean tidal energy takes advantage of the positional changes brought about by seawater relative to the earth\'s rotation, and establishes tidal power plants in coastal areas to convert tidal currents into electrical energy; Ocean wave energy exploits the kinetic energy of water waves transmitted on the sea surface to output electrical energy to the grid; Ocean thermal energy converts the temperature difference in seawater into electrical energy; Ocean biomass energy is realized by using seaweed to transform biomass energy."}{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "How are ocean resources categorized into several types?", "output": "Ocean resources can generally be divided into several types, including energy, petroleum, potash, minerals, food, medicine, and biological resources."}\n{"task_type": "Judgment", "input": "Will the mining of undersea mineral resources have an impact on the marine environment?", "output": "The exploitation of undersea mineral resources may have certain impacts on the marine ecological environment, and it requires corresponding environmental protection measures to address it."}\n', 'reference': 'Ocean energy can be categorized into tidal energy, wave energy, ocean current energy, and thermal energy based on their sources.'}{'question': 'Can the protective casing in undersea cables serve a physical protection role?', 'answer': '\n\nThe protective casing in undersea cables does serve a physical protection role to some extent. According to the provided context, the protective shield is designed to enhance the mechanical strength of the cable and mitigate 