ation", "input": "How to innovate and develop in the field of marine energy technology?", "output": "Technological innovation and development in the field of marine energy can be approached from multiple perspectives, such as strengthening scientific research, enhancing technological innovation and application, establishing platforms for technical exchange, and promoting policy regulations, etc."}\n', 'reference': 'The submarine optical cables in the East China Sea are mainly divided into domestic cables and transnational cables. Domestic cables primarily connect Chinese coastal cities and islands, such as Shanghai, Ningbo, Wenzhou, Fuzhou, Xiamen, etc.; Transnational cables predominantly connect China with countries and regions like Japan, South Korea, the Philippines, Singapore, and Malaysia, with examples including the Asia-Pacific No. 2 cable, and the Japan-China cable, etc.'}{'question': 'Identify the type of ocean circulation in the following diagram: (attached diagram)', 'answer': '\n\nThe database does not contain information about the attached diagram, so I cannot identify the type of ocean circulation it depicts.', 'contexts': 'mate change and so on. Governments of all countries and international organizations are taking steps to strengthen marine environmental protection."}\n{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Categorize and describe the circulation system of the ocean.", "output": "The ocean circulation system is divided into the surface circulation system and the deep-sea circulation system. The surface circulation system is primarily controlled by winds, continental margin currents, and imperfect vortices. The deep-sea circulation system, on the other hand, is driven by density and temperature, influenced by the cold water sources at the ocean floor. These two systems together form a complex ocean circulation, impacting the global climate and ecosystems."}{"task_type": "Recognition", "input": "Identify if the following cables are laid in the east