ated to ensure compliance with maritime laws and sustainable use.  \n\nThe context provided does not elaborate on specific administrative frameworks or policies for managing these rights, so further details on governance mechanisms (e.g., agencies, legal frameworks) are not available in the database.', 'contexts': ' etc., can also cause destruction to the undersea cables. Therefore, regular maintenance and inspection of the undersea cables are highly necessary."}{"task_type": "Extraction", "input": "Extract the range of our country\'s maritime territory and the ownership status of the bird reef islands.", "output": "The scope of our country\'s maritime territory includes territorial seas, contiguous zones, exclusive economic zones, continental shelves, etc. Maritime rights and sovereignty extend to the Diaoyu Islands, the Paracel Islands, the Zhongsha Islands, the Spratly Islands, Huangyan Island, and the Yongshu Reef, among others. Our country advocates maintaining sovereignty rights over these islands and reefs and requires countries or regions claiming sovereignty over the aforementioned islands to respect our rights and status."}{"task_type": "Transformation", "input": "Convert the route of the fishing boat in the ocean into a path on the map.", "output": "The navigation route of the fishing boat in the ocean has been successfully converted into a map display."}\n{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Summarize the limitations and challenges of deep-sea mineral development.", "output": "The development of deep-sea minerals is faced with a series of challenges and limitations, including significant technological difficulties, high environmental risks, and imperfect laws and regulations, among others. Furthermore, the cost of developing deep-sea minerals is extremely high, requiring substantial financial and human resource investment and seeking technological breakthroughs and innovative methods."}\n', 'reference': 'The division and management of the sea area use righ