end a type of marine transportation suitable for use in heavy fog weather.", "output": "Recommend submarines based on weather conditions. They can travel along the seabed in heavy fog weather, maintaining good visibility and safety."}\n{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Provide a brief introduction to the commonly used types of marine forecasts.", "output": "Common types of marine forecasts include: sea condition forecasts, marine meteorological forecasts, tidal forecasts, wave forecasts, sea surface temperature forecasts, ocean current forecasts, marine ecological forecasts, etc."}\n', 'reference': 'The submarine cables in the East China Sea are mainly distributed near coastal cities such as Shanghai, Ningbo, Wenzhou, etc. Among them, the area near Shanghai has the highest density of submarine cables, which are primarily used for communication and power transmission.'}{'question': 'Why is the transmission speed of submarine cables relatively slow?', 'answer': '\n\nThe database does not contain information explaining why the transmission speed of submarine cables is relatively slow. Based on the provided context, submarine cables (particularly optical fibers) are described as high-speed communication lines with large bandwidth and long transmission distances. If the question refers to specific limitations not mentioned in the context, I cannot provide an answer from the given data.', 'contexts': 'important channels connecting offshore oil fields and land, while subsea cables are important communication lines linking various ports and cities."}\n{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Why is the transmission speed of undersea optical cables faster than copper cables?", "output": "The transmission speed of submarine optical cables is faster than that of copper cables mainly because optical cables use light signals for transmission, which results in high signal transmission speed, large bandwidth, and strong interference resistance. In contrast, copper 