igates, submarines, etc.; 4. Research Vessels: mainly include oceanographic survey ships, scientific research ships, etc."}{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Categorize the submarine hydrothermal vents, ore-rich hot springs, and coral reefs.", "output": "Hydrothermal vents and mineral-rich hot springs are part of the undersea hot water zones, while coral reefs fall under marine biology category."}\n', 'reference': 'The types of vessels in the South China Sea include merchant ships, fishing boats, law enforcement boats, research vessels, and others.'}{'question': 'Extract the main fishery resources of the east china sea.', 'answer': '\n\nThe main fishery resources of the East China Sea include **salmon, Spanish mackerel, pomfret, sea bream, cod, crucian carp, carp, and sharks**. These resources are distributed across different regions: Spanish mackerel and sea bream are more abundant in the southern waters, while salmon and cod are more plentiful in the northern waters.', 'contexts': 's in the world. Each year, tens of thousands of ships pass through here, including cargo ships, passenger ships, fishing boats, warships, and more."}\n{"task_type": "Analysis", "input": "Analyze the main fishery resources and their distribution in the east china sea area.", "output": "The main fishing resources in the East China Sea include salmon, Spanish mackerel, pomfret, sea bream, cod, crucian carp, carp, sharks, etc. These fish are distributed in various regions of the East China Sea, for instance, the resources of Spanish mackerel and sea bream are relatively abundant in the southern waters, while salmon and cod resources are more plentiful in the northern waters."}{"task_type": "Recognition", "input": "Identify the name of the submarine cable connecting mainland china and taiwan.", "output": "The undersea cable connecting mainland China and Taiwan is named \\"Strait Fiber-optic Cable\\". This cable is an important communication line between mainland China and Taiwan, carrying a large amount of telephone, internet, and data transmission services. The construction and operation of the Strait Fiber-optic Cable have played a crucial role in promoting economic exchange and information communication between the two sides of the strait."}\n', 'reference': 'The main fishery resources in the East China Sea include yellow croaker, pomfret, porgy, carp, mackerel, mullet, cod, etc. Among them, yellow croaker, pomfret, porgy, and carp are the main fishery resources in the northern area of the East China Sea, while mackerel, mullet, cod, and others are mainly distributed in the southeast area of the East China Sea.'}{'question': 'Introduce a method of making cosmetics using marine green resources.', 'answer': '\n\nA method of making cosmetics using marine green resources involves utilizing **seaweed essence**. Seaweed is rich in active colloids that help the skin retain moisture, improve elasticity and softness, and aid in removing excess oils and toxins. This natural ingredient is extracted and incorporated into cosmetic formulations to provide nourishing and purifying benefits. \n\n*(Note: The provided context only mentions this specific method related to seaweed. Information on other marine green resource applications for cosmetics is not included in the database.)*', 'contexts': 'rengthening supervision and management, fostering a mindset of ocean conservation, and minimizing the environmental impact caused by human factors."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "Introduce a method of making cosmetics using marine green resources.", "output": "A method of producing cosmetics using marine green resources involves the use of seaweed essence. Seaweed contains active colloids that can help the skin retain moisture, enhance elasticity and softness, and assist in the removal of skin oils and toxins."}{"task_type": "Extraction", "input": "Extract three evaluation indicators from the guide provided on the official website of the ocean environment evaluation center.", "output": "Index 1: Physicochemical indicators of the marine environment, including temperature, salinity, pH, dissolved oxygen, nutrients, etc.;\\nIndex 2: Indicators of marine ecosystems, including biodiversity, protection of species, etc.;\\nIndex 3: Marine environment safety indicators, including marine pollution, coastal zone degradation, etc."}\n{"task_type": "Judgment", "input": "Determine whether the mineral resources in the east china sea area are abundant.", "output": "The mineral resources in the East China Sea are very abundant, among which natural gas and oil are the most important mineral resources. In addition, the East China Sea area also has a variety of mineral resources such as phosphate, manganese, copper, lead and zinc."}\n', 'reference': 'A method of producing cosmetics using marine green resources involves the use of seaweed essence. Seaweed contains active colloids that can help the skin retain moisture, enhance elasticity and softness, and assist in the removal of skin oils and toxins.'}{'question': 'Write a proposal letter to china telecom regarding the construction and maintenance of submarine cables in the east china sea.', 'answer': "\n\n**Proposal Letter to China Telecom**  \n**Subject: Proposal for the Construction and Maintenance of Submarine Cables in the East China Sea**  \n\nDear [Recipient's Name/Title],  \n\nI am writing to propose a collaborative initiative with China Telecom to advance the construction and long-term maintenance of submarine cables in the East China Sea, a region of critical strategic and economic importance for China’s telecommunications infrastructure.  \n\nThe East China Sea is a vital corridor for subsea cable networks, hosting key systems such as China Telecom’s East China Sea Submarine Optical Cable, alongside international networks like the Asia Pacific Cable Network (APCN) and Asia Pacific Gateway (APG). These cables underpin regional communications, data transmission, and digital connectivity, making their reliability and resilience essential.  \n\n**Proposed Initiatives:**  \n1. **Strategic Construction:**  \n   - Develop a scientifically planned expansion of submarine cable infrastructure, prioritizing routes that minimize ecological disruption while maximizing redundancy and capacity.  \n   - Leverage advanced materials and engineering techniques to enhance cable durability against environmental stressors (e.g., seismic activity, marine currents).  \n\n2. **Environmental Stewardship:**  \n   - Conduct rigorous environmental impact assessments (EIAs) prior to deployment to safeguard marine ecosystems.  \n   - Adopt eco-friendly construction practices, such as low-impact trenching and biodegradable protective coatings, to mitigate long-term ecological risks.  \n\n3. **Maintenance & Innovation:**  \n   - Establish a dedicated maintenance team equipped with AI-driven monitoring systems and autonomous underwater vehicles (AUVs) for real-time fault detection and rapid repairs.  \n   - Invest in R&D for next-generation technologies, including self-healing cables and energy-efficient repeaters, to future-proof the network.  \n\n4. **Collaborative Governance:**  \n   - Partner with maritime authorities, environmental agencies, and international stakeholders to align with regional regulations and best practices.  \n   - Develop a shared maintenance protocol with operators like China Unicom to ensure cross-network resilience.  \n\nThis initiative will not only strengthen China Telecom’s leadership in critical infrastructure but also contribute to the sustainable development of the East China Sea’s digital ecosystem. I request the opportunity to discuss this proposal in detail and explore how China Telecom can lead or collaborate on this endeavor.  \n\nPlease let me know a convenient time for a meeting, and I will provide supplementary technical and financial documentation.  \n\nSincerely,  \n[Your Full Name]  \n[Your Position/Organization]  \n[Contact Information]  \n\n---  \n*Note: This proposal integrates insights from existing East China Sea cable projects and emphasizes environmental, technical, and strategic priorities outlined in the provided context.*", 'contexts': 'tides into mechanical energy, then using hydraulic machinery to transform the mechanical energy into electrical energy to achieve power generation."}\n{"task_type": "Letter Writing", "input": "Write a proposal letter regarding the laying of submarine cable in the east china sea area.", "output": "Dear Leader: I believe that the laying of undersea cables in the East China Sea holds important strategic significance and economic value. However, during the deployment process, it is vital to fully consider environmental protection and sustainable development factors to prevent irreversible damage to the marine ecosystem. At the same time, there is a need to strengthen technical research and development and personnel training to enhance the scientific and technological content and efficiency of undersea cables. I hope that you can attach importance to this issue, formulate a scientific and reasonable deployment plan, and promote better results in the laying of undersea cables in the East China Sea."}{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Edit an article about the undersea cables in the east china sea area.", "output": "The East China Sea is one of China\'s key areas for subsea cable layout, with multiple submarine cables running through this area, providing critical support for local communications and data transmission. Among them, the East China Sea submarine optical cable of China Telecom and the East China Sea submarine optical cable of China Unicom are the two main submarine optical cables within the East China Sea. In addition, submarine cables like the Asia Pacific Cable Network (APCN) and Asia Pacific Gateway (APG) also traverse the East China Sea."}\n', 'reference': 'Dear Leaders of China Telecom: I am a marine scientist and I have some 