ables, regular check-up and maintenance, and the use of new materials etc."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "May I ask, what are the advantages of marine energy technology?\\n", "output": "Compared to other forms of energy, marine energy technology has the following advantages: it\'s renewable, stable, low carbon, environmentally friendly, and has a wide coverage. Moreover, marine energy technology can be combined with other forms of energy, making the energy supply more stable and reliable."}{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Edit a technical plan for the development of marine energy.", "output": "The marine energy development technology plan should include the type of marine energy development, development area, equipment selection, installation methods, operation and maintenance management, etc."}\n{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Write an informative article introducing the underwater topography.", "output": "The undersea terrain is one of the largest unknown areas on the surface of the Earth. The underwater topography includes many complex and unusual environments, such as seamounts, oceanic trenches, and underwater volcanoes. These terrains have significant impacts on the evolution of life and the formation of ecosystems."}\n', 'reference': 'The current development of marine energy technology is increasingly mature, such as the utilization of tides, ocean currents, and waves for power generation has been well applied and promoted. Meanwhile, new technologies and models continue to emerge.'}{'question': 'Write a letter introducing the submarine topography and terrain of the east china sea.', 'answer': '\n\nDear Mr./Ms. XX:  \n\nThe submarine topography and terrain of the East China Sea are characterized by a complex and diverse landscape. The seabed features include seamounts, trenches, ridges, plateaus, and hillocks. Notably, the seamounts in the central East China Sea, formed by volcanic activity, are among the region’s most significant under