ication and optimization of these technologies** may be key areas for development. For more specific trends (e.g., efficiency improvements, cost reduction, or hybrid systems), the database does not provide sufficient details.', 'contexts': ' In the future, we need to further improve the standardization of marine engineering to promote the development of the marine engineering industry."}\n{"task_type": "Recommendation", "input": "Could you recommend some classic books related to marine ecology?", "output": "I recommend books such as \\"Basic Principles of Marine Ecology\\", \\"Marine Particles and Ecological Models\\", and \\"Oceanography\\"."}{"task_type": "Extraction", "input": "Extract a few types of renewable marine energy technologies.", "output": "Tidal energy, wave power, ocean thermal energy conversion, and ocean wave energy are four renewable marine energy technologies. Tidal energy utilizes the electricity generated by tidal movement; wave power harnesses electricity from the up and down motion of sea surfaces; ocean thermal energy conversion mainly generates electricity exploiting differences in seawater temperature; ocean wave energy transforms the mechanical energy of sea waves into electricity. These technologies possess broad application prospects, offering effective solutions for energy issues."}\n', 'reference': 'The future development trend of marine energy technology is diversification, high efficiency, intelligence, and integration, and it will continue to innovate and improve in specific applications.'}{'question': 'Briefly describe the principle of seawater precipitation.', 'answer': "\n\nThe database does not contain information about the principle of seawater precipitation. I don't know.", 'contexts': ' and wavelengths, its scattering, transmission, and absorption properties vary, which is the fundamental law of the optical properties of seawater."}\n{"task_type": "Letter Writing", "input": "Write a letter to the local government, suggesting 