, sharks, etc. These fish resources are of great significance to the fisheries and economic development of our country."}\n{"task_type": "Extraction", "input": "What major breakthroughs in ocean exploration technology has China achieved?", "output": "Our country has made many significant breakthroughs in marine detection technology, including multi-beam depth measuring ships, seabed observation networks, abyssal acoustic detectors, and abyssal drilling ships, etc."}{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Draft a construction plan for the undersea optic cable in the east china sea.", "output": "East Sea Submarine Cable Construction Scheme: Firstly, a survey and assessment of the seabed topography and marine ecological environment is required to determine the layout plan of the cable. Secondly, a suitable cable type and technology should be chosen for the design and manufacture of the cable. Lastly, the cable should be laid and maintained to ensure stable operation."}\n{"task_type": "Transformation", "input": "Convert the length of the undersea cable in the east china sea from kilometers to nautical miles.", "output": "The length of the submarine cable in the East China Sea is approximately 5000 kilometers, which is about 2700 nautical miles when converted. The nautical mile is a unit of marine mileage, with 1 nautical mile roughly equivalent to 1.852 kilometers. Therefore, the length of the submarine cable in the East China Sea is about 2700 nautical miles."}\n', 'reference': 'Our country has made many significant breakthroughs in marine detection technology, including multi-beam depth measuring ships, seabed observation networks, abyssal acoustic detectors, and abyssal drilling ships, etc.'}{'question': 'Is the Great Oceanic Circulation a component of the oceanic dynamic system?', 'answer': '\n\nYes, the Great Oceanic Circulation is a component of the oceanic dynamic system. The oceanic dynamical system encompasses natural forces and processes that drive marine circulati