., ocean acidification or biodiversity loss), so further research is required for a comprehensive understanding.', 'contexts': 'ure, it is necessary to strengthen technological research and development and environmental protection measures to achieve sustainable development."}\n{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Explain why changes in the seabed topography have a significant impact on the environment and the ecosystem.", "output": "Changes in the seafloor topography can alter the seafloor ecological environment, resulting in changes in the composition, distribution, and quantity of organisms such as fish, seaweed, and coral in the marine ecosystem. Meanwhile, it can also adversely affect the growth and reproduction of marine organisms. Changes in the seafloor topography can be influenced by atmospheric conditions as well. Extreme weather events like storm surges and hurricanes contribute to changes in seafloor topography.\\n"}{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "Briefly elaborate on the current status and trends of green development in the ocean.", "output": "With the rapid growth of the global economy and population, marine green development has become one of the global hotspots. In the future, the marine green industry will continue to grow and become an important support for achieving sustainable marine development."}\n{"task_type": "Extraction", "input": "Extract the relevant data of sea ice.", "output": "The relevant data of sea ice includes variables such as sea surface temperature, sea surface height, salinity of sea water, and ocean current speed."}\n', 'reference': 'The impact of marine climate change on global ecosystems is extremely complex, including alterations in ecosystem structure and function, variations in species distribution and quantity, and the evolution of coastal terrestrial ecosystems.'}{'question': 'Edit an article introducing polar shipping.', 'answer': "\n\nThe database does not contain the necessary information 