ds?", "output": "National standards inquiries can be made on the Standard Information Inquiry Platform of the National Standardization Management Committee."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "Why does the disappearance of sea ice affect the polar ecosystem?", "output": "The disappearance of sea ice would impact the polar ecosystem, as sea ice is one of the most crucial ecological factors in polar marine habitats. It provides living, breeding, and resting conditions for various organisms such as fish, seabirds, and mammals. The loss of sea ice could lead to changes in species diversity and ecological imbalance."}\n', 'reference': 'The disappearance of sea ice would impact the polar ecosystem, as sea ice is one of the most crucial ecological factors in polar marine habitats. It provides living, breeding, and resting conditions for various organisms such as fish, seabirds, and mammals. The loss of sea ice could lead to changes in species diversity and ecological imbalance.'}{'question': 'Describe the status of submarine cable resource development in the east china sea area.', 'answer': "\n\nThe development of submarine cable resources in the East China Sea area is relatively advanced, with significant infrastructure in communication, power, and oil/gas sectors. In the communication sector, subsea fiber optic cables primarily connect mainland China, Taiwan, and Japan, facilitating transnational data and telecommunications. Power subsea cables also play a critical role, linking the power grids of these regions to support energy distribution. Additionally, the area features subsea pipelines in the oil and gas industry, used for transporting oil and natural gas. These cables and pipelines highlight the East China Sea's strategic importance in regional energy and communication networks.", 'contexts': 'n addition, it is also necessary to strengthen island safety and preventive measures to ensure the rational use and protection of island resources."}\n{"task_typ