 from the provided context.', 'contexts': 'e can understand the characteristics and trends of the marine environment in this area. It also helps to discover potential resources and problems."}\n{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Categorize the fishery resources in the east china sea into which types?", "output": "The fishery resources of the East China Sea can be divided into three categories: large, medium, and small-sized fish. The large-sized category includes fish such as halibut, carp, and grass carp; the medium-sized category includes catfish, cod and so on; and the small-sized category includes abalone, sea cucumber, crab, etc."}{"task_type": "Description", "input": "What are the famous islands in the East China Sea?", "output": "The East China Sea area is home to numerous offshore islands, such as Xiashima Island in Shandong Province, the Beikyushu Islands, the Yangtze River Estuary Islands, the Laizhou Bay Islands, the Yellow Sea Islands, and so on. Among them, the Fushan Islands in the dredging area of Lianyungang, boasting beaches, reefs, and corals, are also known as Coral Islands. They constitute a marine ecosystem of excellent condition."}\n', 'reference': 'The primary fish resources in the East China Sea area include marine cyprinid fish, turtles, shrimp and crab shellfish, and other fish. Among them, the marine cyprinid fish category mainly includes carp, grass carp, catfish, and other fish. Turtles include soft-shelled turtles, turtles, and tortoises, etc. Shrimp and crab shellfish consist of mussels, yellow croaker, crayfish, green crab, etc. Other fish like hairtail, horse mackerel, and marlin are also included. These fish resources can not only meet domestic consumption needs but also have significant export potential.'}{'question': 'Describe the types and quantity of vessels in the east china sea area.', 'answer': '\n\nThe East China Sea area includes various vessel types such as cargo ships (most common, for goods transportation), passen