eet rising demand. Future efforts will likely focus on integrating advanced technologies to improve efficiency and resilience against environmental challenges.  \n\nThe construction of submarine cables in the East China Sea underscores China’s commitment to modernizing its maritime infrastructure. By prioritizing innovation and sustainability, these projects are poised to drive economic development and regional cooperation in the years ahead.  \n\n*Note: This article synthesizes publicly available information and general industry knowledge, as specific project details may not be fully disclosed in the provided context.*', 'contexts': ' locations in the east sea area.", "output": "The undersea cables in the East China Sea are mainly laid out in areas such as Shanghai and Zhejiang."}\n{"task_type": "Letter Writing", "input": "Write a letter to a certain marine company, introducing the construction situation of the undersea pipeline in the east china sea.", "output": "Dear Leader of the Certain Ocean Company: Our company has made some progress in the construction of submarine pipelines in the East China Sea area. At present, we have completed the construction of several submarine pipelines, mainly for the transportation of natural gas and oil. In the future, we will continue to intensify the construction of submarine pipelines to make a greater contribution to the energy supply in the East China Sea area. Thank you!"}{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Classify the submarine cables according to the transmission medium.", "output": "Submarine cables can be classified into optical cables, electrical cables, communication cables, etc., based on the transmission medium."}\n', 'reference': "The construction of undersea cables in the East China Sea is an important part of our country's information infrastructure. Undersea cables can be used for undersea communication, marine observation and other fields, but also for environmental protection work such as undersea waste